{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Last summer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the birds living on Town Lake were geese, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> were swans, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> were herons, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af59f5a81354c1925a58cb897e1d142111b1d7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> were ducks. What percent of the birds that were not swans were geese?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cd607f22e7436a0effc23144aa6c58a2d5cfef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 40 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To simplify the problem, WLOG, let us say that there were a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> birds. The number of birds that are not swans is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The number of geese is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the percentage is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/3731b1626c6fe7b747e2dfdc20165442ec880b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{75} \\times 100 = 40 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"168\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A\">2011 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<t